{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Church Directory (prototype) | Mere Orthodoxy</title>
{{!-- noindex because this is an internal review prototype whose
      listings no church has confirmed. It must never be found in search,
      and it must never be mistaken for a directory a reader could rely
      on. Same pattern as custom-welcome.hbs and custom-migrate.hbs. --}}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
<meta name="description" content="A prototype church directory for Mere Orthodoxy readers. The churches in it were named by members and have not confirmed their listings." />
<meta property="og:title" content="Church Directory (prototype)" />
<meta property="og:description" content="A prototype church directory for Mere Orthodoxy readers. The churches in it were named by members and have not confirmed their listings." />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Church Directory (prototype)" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="A prototype church directory for Mere Orthodoxy readers. The churches in it were named by members and have not confirmed their listings." />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "css/church-directory.css"}}&amp;frv=church-directory-20261103b" />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- Church Directory prototype (Ian, 2026-11-02). For internal review
     only: there is no routes.yaml entry, so the page exists only where
     Ghost Admin assigns this template to a page, and the intent is that
     it stays a draft and is read through Preview.

     WHAT IS REAL AND WHAT IS NOT (Ian, 2026-11-03: use the real list).
     The listings (assets/data/church-directory.json) are the churches
     members named when they confirmed a mailing address: a name as they
     typed it and a country, nothing more. No church has confirmed its
     listing, there are no cities, addresses or service times, and a
     tradition shows only where the church's own name states it. The form
     sends nowhere. The prototype notice under the header says both of
     those things on every view, and it is the one piece of copy on the
     page that may not be softened.

     WHERE THE PINS COME FROM (Ian, 2026-11-03: "show the map"). The only
     place stored beside a church's name is the member's own address, which
     is not the church's, so it is never used as a location. Instead each
     name was looked up on OpenStreetMap once, at build time, with the
     member's state only as a search hint. A pin was kept only where OSM
     tags exactly one place of worship by that name in that state, and four
     matches whose names did not agree were thrown out by hand. That pins
     46 of the 152 and gives those 46 a city and state; the rest stay in
     the list with no pin. OSM's licence (ODbL) requires the credit in both
     map captions. The page itself still fetches nothing from OSM.

     NO NETWORK BEYOND THIS SITE'S OWN ASSETS. Two fetches, both static
     files under /assets/data/: the listings and the map outlines.
     No worker, no Ghost API, no form endpoint, no map tiles. A reviewer
     can read the whole page in Network and see those two requests.

     THE MAP IS DRAWN HERE, NOT EMBEDDED (Ian, 2026-11-02: "make an
     actual map"). A tile map means a third-party host in connect-src and
     img-src and a request per tile, which is both a network call this
     prototype must not make and a CSP change it must not need. So the
     outlines are a static file (assets/data/church-directory-map.json,
     public-domain Natural Earth countries and US Census states, built
     once and simplified) and church-directory.js draws them as inline
     SVG, with a pin per church at the latitude and longitude in the
     listing. The map follows the filters and zooms to what they leave.
     It is a picture of the list, not a second way through it: the pins
     are not in the tab order, and the list below has every church on
     the map with the same link.

     THREE VIEWS IN ONE TEMPLATE, SWITCHED BY THE HASH. A Ghost draft
     preview has no routes under it, so a church cannot have its own
     path. The hash is what is left: "" is the directory, #church/<slug>
     is one church, #add and #claim/<slug> are the form. All three are
     in the markup here and two are `hidden`; church-directory.js shows
     one at a time. `hidden` takes a view out of the accessibility tree
     as well as off the screen, so the page always has exactly one h1
     that anyone can reach.

     THE FORM IS WRITTEN OUT HERE RATHER THAN BUILT IN JS. It is the
     site's own stacked form, and the classes that style it
     (.stacked-form, .form-group, .form-legend, .form-field, .form-row)
     are all scoped under .membership-support in screen.css, which is
     why <main> carries that class. Written as markup, the form reads as
     the same form as /groups/ and /gift/; built in JS, it would be a
     pile of createElement calls nobody could compare against them.
     Only DATA is built in JS, and only with textContent.

     .cd ON <main> IS THE PAGE'S OWN NAMESPACE. Every class this page
     adds is prefixed cd-, and every rule in church-directory.css is
     scoped under .cd, so nothing here can reach the rest of the site
     and nothing in screen.css has to be touched to style it. --}}

<main class="membership-support cd">

  {{!-- Every view, directly under the site header, and deliberately not
        dismissible. A reviewer who lands on #church/<slug> from a link
        must see it as plainly as one who lands on the directory. --}}
  <p class="cd-notice">This is a prototype. These churches were named by Mere Orthodoxy members and have not confirmed their listings. Nothing you enter is sent or saved.</p>

  <noscript>
    <p class="cd-noscript">This prototype needs JavaScript to show the directory.</p>
  </noscript>

  {{!-- ───────────────────────── Directory ───────────────────────── --}}
  <div class="cd-view" data-cd-view="directory">

    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Church Directory</p>
        <h1 class="page-hero-headline" id="cd-directory-title" tabindex="-1">Find a church where <em>Mere&nbsp;Orthodoxy</em> readers worship.</h1>
        <p class="page-hero-sub">Churches named by Mere Orthodoxy members, so readers who move or travel can find a congregation.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cd-body">
      <div class="container">

        {{!-- Real labels and real controls. The contributors alphabet
              rail is the look being mirrored (the 11px tracked label and
              the hairline under the strip), not the pills: a pill row
              cannot say which of four things it is filtering, and four
              filters need four names. --}}
        <div class="cd-filters">
          <div class="cd-filter">
            <label class="cd-filter-label" for="cd-q">Search</label>
            <input type="search" id="cd-q" class="cd-input" data-cd-q autocomplete="off" placeholder="Church name or city" />
          </div>
          <div class="cd-filter">
            <label class="cd-filter-label" for="cd-country">Country</label>
            <select id="cd-country" class="cd-select" data-cd-country></select>
          </div>
          <div class="cd-filter" data-cd-state-filter hidden>
            <label class="cd-filter-label" for="cd-state">State or province</label>
            <select id="cd-state" class="cd-select" data-cd-state></select>
          </div>
          <div class="cd-filter">
            <label class="cd-filter-label" for="cd-city">City</label>
            <select id="cd-city" class="cd-select" data-cd-city></select>
          </div>
          <div class="cd-filter">
            <label class="cd-filter-label" for="cd-tradition">Tradition</label>
            <select id="cd-tradition" class="cd-select" data-cd-tradition></select>
          </div>
          <div class="cd-filter cd-filter--clear">
            <button type="button" class="cd-clear" data-cd-clear hidden>Clear filters</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="cd-count" data-cd-count role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

        {{!-- Hidden until the outlines have loaded and at least one
              listing has a place to pin. A listing with no coordinates
              is still in the list; it is just not on the map. --}}
        <figure class="cd-map" data-cd-map hidden>
          <div class="cd-map-frame" data-cd-map-frame></div>
          {{!-- Shown only after a cluster has zoomed the map in. --}}
          <button type="button" class="cd-map-reset" data-cd-map-reset hidden>Show the whole map</button>
          <figcaption class="cd-map-caption" data-cd-map-caption></figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="cd-list" data-cd-list></div>

      </div>
    </section>

    {{!-- The site divides a page from the band that follows it with the
          round site mark. One mark, between the listings and the ask. --}}
    <div class="cd-ornament">{{> "flourish-mark"}}</div>

    <section class="cd-add-band">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="cd-add-heading">Add your church</h2>
        <p class="cd-add-sub">Pastors and church staff can list their congregation. We confirm every listing with the church before it appears.</p>
        <p class="cd-add-action"><a class="btn btn-solid btn-lg" href="#add" data-cd-link>Add your church</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  {{!-- ──────────────────────── One church ──────────────────────── --}}
  <div class="cd-view" data-cd-view="church" hidden>
    <section class="cd-detail">
      <div class="container">

        {{!-- href is rewritten by the script to carry the filters the
              reader had set, so Back does not drop them. --}}
        <p class="cd-back"><a href="#" data-cd-back>Back to the directory</a></p>

        <h1 class="cd-detail-name" data-cd-detail-name id="cd-church-title" tabindex="-1"></h1>
        <p class="cd-detail-place" data-cd-detail-place></p>
        <p class="cd-detail-badges"><span class="cd-badge">Unconfirmed</span></p>
        <p class="cd-detail-description" data-cd-detail-description></p>

        <dl class="cd-detail-facts">
          <dt>Tradition</dt><dd data-cd-detail-tradition></dd>
          <dt>Service times</dt><dd data-cd-detail-times></dd>
          <dt>Address</dt><dd data-cd-detail-address></dd>
          <dt>Website</dt><dd data-cd-detail-website></dd>
        </dl>
        <figure class="cd-map cd-map--detail" data-cd-detail-map hidden>
          <div class="cd-map-frame" data-cd-detail-map-frame></div>
          <figcaption class="cd-map-caption">The pin marks where this church appears on OpenStreetMap. Church locations © OpenStreetMap contributors.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="cd-claim-panel">
          <h2 class="cd-claim-heading">Is this your church?</h2>
          <p class="cd-claim-sub">Pastors and church staff can correct a listing or claim it.</p>
          <p><a class="btn btn-solid" href="#add" data-cd-claim-link>Claim this listing</a></p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  {{!-- ───────────────────── Add or claim form ───────────────────── --}}
  <div class="cd-view" data-cd-view="form" hidden>

    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Church Directory</p>
        <h1 class="page-hero-headline" id="cd-form-title" tabindex="-1" data-cd-form-title>Add your church</h1>
        <p class="page-hero-sub" data-cd-form-sub>Tell us about the congregation. We confirm every listing with the church before it appears.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="form-section">
      <div class="container">

        {{!-- novalidate: the browser's own bubbles cannot be placed under
              a field or tied to it with aria-describedby, and they stop
              at the first bad field rather than listing them. The script
              validates and writes the messages itself. --}}
        <form class="stacked-form cd-form" data-cd-form novalidate>

          <div class="cd-form-summary" data-cd-summary hidden>
            <h2 class="cd-form-summary-heading" data-cd-summary-heading tabindex="-1">Check these fields</h2>
            <ul class="cd-form-summary-list" data-cd-summary-list></ul>
          </div>

          <p class="cd-form-claiming" data-cd-claiming hidden></p>

          {{!-- Each field is a <div> holding a <label for>, not a wrapping
                <label>. A wrapping label makes everything inside it part of
                the control's name, so a screen reader announced "Church name,
                Enter the name of the church" and then read the error again
                from aria-describedby. Errors and hints sit beside the label
                and are tied to the control by id. The screen.css form set is
                styled by class, so the change is invisible. --}}
          <fieldset class="form-group">
            <legend class="form-legend">Your church</legend>

            <div class="form-field">
              <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-church_name">Church name</label>
              <input type="text" id="cd-f-church_name" name="church_name" data-cd-field="church_name" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="cd-err-church_name" />
              <span class="cd-error" id="cd-err-church_name" data-cd-error="church_name"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="form-field">
              <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-address">Street address (optional)</label>
              <input type="text" id="cd-f-address" name="address" data-cd-field="address" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>

            <div class="form-row">
              <div class="form-field">
                <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-city">City</label>
                <input type="text" id="cd-f-city" name="city" data-cd-field="city" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="cd-err-city" />
                <span class="cd-error" id="cd-err-city" data-cd-error="city"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="form-field">
                <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-state">State or province (optional)</label>
                <input type="text" id="cd-f-state" name="state" data-cd-field="state" aria-describedby="cd-hint-state" />
                <span class="form-hint" id="cd-hint-state">Leave this empty if your country has none.</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="form-row">
              <div class="form-field">
                <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-country">Country</label>
                <select id="cd-f-country" name="country" data-cd-field="country" data-cd-country-select aria-required="true" aria-describedby="cd-err-country"></select>
                <span class="cd-error" id="cd-err-country" data-cd-error="country"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="form-field">
                <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-tradition">Tradition (optional)</label>
                <select id="cd-f-tradition" name="tradition" data-cd-field="tradition" data-cd-tradition-select></select>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="form-field">
              <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-website">Website (optional)</label>
              <input type="url" id="cd-f-website" name="website" data-cd-field="website" placeholder="https://" />
            </div>

            <div class="form-field">
              <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-service_times">Service times (optional)</label>
              <input type="text" id="cd-f-service_times" name="service_times" data-cd-field="service_times" placeholder="Sunday 10:30 a.m." />
            </div>

            {{!-- No aria-live on the count. Live, it read "297 characters
                  left" after every letter. As a description it is read
                  when the reader lands on the field and asks for it. --}}
            <div class="form-field">
              <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-description">Short description (optional)</label>
              <textarea id="cd-f-description" name="description" data-cd-field="description" maxlength="300" rows="4" aria-describedby="cd-count-description"></textarea>
              <span class="form-hint" id="cd-count-description" data-cd-char>300 characters left</span>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset class="form-group">
            <legend class="form-legend">You</legend>

            <div class="form-row">
              <div class="form-field">
                <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-your_name">Your name</label>
                <input type="text" id="cd-f-your_name" name="your_name" data-cd-field="your_name" autocomplete="name" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="cd-err-your_name" />
                <span class="cd-error" id="cd-err-your_name" data-cd-error="your_name"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="form-field">
                <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-email">Email</label>
                <input type="email" id="cd-f-email" name="email" data-cd-field="email" autocomplete="email" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="cd-err-email" />
                <span class="cd-error" id="cd-err-email" data-cd-error="email"></span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="form-field">
              <label class="form-label" for="cd-f-role">Your role</label>
              <select id="cd-f-role" name="role" data-cd-field="role">
                <option value="Pastor">Pastor</option>
                <option value="Church staff">Church staff</option>
                <option value="Elder or deacon">Elder or deacon</option>
                <option value="Member">Member</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <div class="cd-consent">
              <label class="cd-consent-label">
                <input type="checkbox" name="authorized" data-cd-field="authorized" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="cd-err-authorized" />
                <span>I'm authorized to list this church, and the church agrees to appear in the directory.</span>
              </label>
              <span class="cd-error" id="cd-err-authorized" data-cd-error="authorized"></span>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-solid btn-lg cd-submit">Send for confirmation</button>
          <p class="cd-form-note">Prototype: this form does not send or save anything.</p>
        </form>

        {{!-- Replaces the form on submit. Written here rather than built
              in JS so its copy is reviewable in the template. --}}
        <div class="cd-done" data-cd-done hidden>
          <h2 class="cd-done-heading" data-cd-done-heading tabindex="-1">Thanks. Check your email.</h2>
          <p>In the real directory, we'd send you a link to confirm the listing. Nothing appears until the church confirms it.</p>
          <p class="cd-form-note">Prototype: this form did not send or save anything.</p>
          <p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="#" data-cd-back>Back to the directory</a></p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script src="{{asset "js/page/church-directory.js"}}&amp;frv=church-directory-20261103b"></script>
</main>
